      "notes": [
        "Issue: the Vue quickstart only sets up CopilotKit's own BuiltInAgent; it never connects an OpenAI Agents SDK agent (no HttpAgent, no Python agent), and its \"use your framework's quickstart\" callout points back at this same page."
      ],
      "block": null,
      "links": [
        {
          "text": null,
          "clip": "OAI-vue-01-Quickstart",
          "loom": "https://www.loom.com/share/41698cc95c884c82a595069ca3cc2f17",
          "narration": {
            "clip": "OAI-vue-01-Quickstart",
            "segments": [
              {
                "at": "doc",
                "text": "Ok so this is the quickstart page for Vue with OpenAI Agents, and I'm reporting a problem on this page."
              },
              {
                "at": "evidence",
                "text": "This is the problem, umm, the page only sets up BuiltInAgent, and says not to use it if you already have an agent."
              },
              {
                "at": "evidence#2",
                "text": "And it says to use your framework's quickstart for the wiring, but, uh, this is that quickstart."
              },
              {
                "at": "ide",
                "text": "This is my project, I've implemented the exact code from the doc."
              },
              {
                "at": "demo",
                "text": "Moving on to the demo. The chat does reply, but it's CopilotKit's built-in agent, not an OpenAI Agents agent."
              },
              {
                "at": "notepad",
                "text": "So basically, the page should connect a Vue app to an OpenAI Agents SDK agent, but there's no agent wiring and no Python agent at all."
              },
              {
                "at": "+",
                "text": "So this needs a fix, kindly check it."
              }
            ]
          },
